WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.379 --> 00:00:03.510
Chinese President Xi Jinping calls it the

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.341
project of the century.

00:00:05.341 --> 00:00:08.240
China's sprawling belt
and road initiative,

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.513
sometimes called the New Silk Road.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.230
Measured in today's dollars
it has already cost more

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.520
than the US Marshal
Plan that rebuilt Europe

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.080
after World War II.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.901
The World Bank estimates
that some $575 billion

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:26.350
worth of energy plants, railways, roads,

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.430
ports, and other projects have been built

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.910
or are in the works.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.800
With 130 nations signing
deals or expressing interest

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.840
from power plants in Pakistan
to a high speed rail line

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.944
in Indonesia it's one
of the most ambitious

00:00:37.944 --> 00:00:41.923
intercontinental infrastructure
projects in human history.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.610
The stakes for the belt and
road project are astronomical.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.770
Both monetarily as Morgan
Stanley estimates spending will

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:55.140
total $1.3 trillion by 2027.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.050
And for China's global
image on the world stage.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.462
China would like to make a
deal much more than I would.

00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:02.760
As President Donald Trump scales back

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.320
US involvement in
international trade agreements

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.800
Xi is using the belt and
road to position himself

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.770
as the champion of global
cooperation, development,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.070
and free trade.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.326
But the project is not
without its critics.

00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:18.630
There are accusations that
China is luring poorer countries

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.600
into debt traps for its own political

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.760
and strategic gain.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.540
With some countries even
downsizing or completely

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.850
canceling projects even as
new deals are being signed.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.550
Several countries have had
to rethink their involvement.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:33.630
Often after popular backlash
or change of government,

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.570
or both.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.960
For example Sri Lanka
borrowed $8 billion to build

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.100
a new port, couldn't repay the loans,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.630
and then gave a
state-owned Chinese company

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.840
a 99 year lease in
exchange for debt relief.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.345
The port has little business
now but provides China

00:01:48.345 --> 00:01:51.658
a strategic berth along
key shipping lanes.

00:01:51.658 --> 00:01:55.100
Myanmar also drastically
scaled back a port deal

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.310
struck under its previous military regime.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.945
Originally to $7.5 billion
reduced to just $1.3 billion.

00:02:01.945 --> 00:02:04.820
China would like to get
somewhat of a roll back.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.380
The Trump administration has sought to

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.766
capitalize on the doubts with
Vice President Mike Pence

00:02:08.766 --> 00:02:11.966
telling southeast Asian
nations the US would not offer

00:02:11.966 --> 00:02:15.124
a constricting belt or a one way road.

00:02:15.124 --> 00:02:18.550
In the face of criticism
President Xi is doing

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.620
damage control.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.150
Calling the project a road for peace.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:25.166
In 2018 the initiative
extended into South America,

00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:28.040
the Caribbean, and even the Arctic.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:31.040
In 2019 Italy became the
first group of seven nation

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.418
to sign up, brushing off
warnings from both American

00:02:33.418 --> 00:02:35.326
and European allies.

00:02:35.326 --> 00:02:37.910
In Asia these are the
countries that approve

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.570
of the belt and road project.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.825
These are cautious, and these are opposed.

00:02:42.825 --> 00:02:45.486
Overall the World Bank
says the revived silk road

00:02:45.486 --> 00:02:48.583
has the potential to
stimulate economic growth.

00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:51.550
But with that growth comes challenges.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.130
Some of the risks include
allegations of corruption

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:57.040
like those the Kyrgyzstan
Prime Minister is facing

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.280
and potential for environmental damage.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.145
Which prompted a Kenyan
court to order a halt to

00:03:01.145 --> 00:03:03.990
a power plant being built on Lamu Island,

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.898
a major tourist destination.

00:03:05.898 --> 00:03:09.684
Xi, who is dealing with
China's own debt problems

00:03:09.684 --> 00:03:13.010
and slowing economic growth
has promised debt relief

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.800
to some African nations.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.040
And a top Chinese regulator
called for greater

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.945
social responsibility
in overseas investments.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:23.696
That's the kind of sensitivity
China will need to show

00:03:23.696 --> 00:03:27.312
and follow through on if it's
to win over their skeptics.

